# Multipolygon relations: drawn with holes, selected by double-clicking inside
# their fill, and kept correct when a member node moves.
#
# Coordinate model: the viewport center is at window (488, 388) — see
# select.osmscript for the derivation. fixtures/multipolygon.osm is laid out in
# window coordinates at zoom 18, centered on (40.7120, -74.0060):
#   A  Mirror Lake, relation 7001 (natural=water): outer way 6001 spanning
#      x 90..430, y 80..340, and the island, way 6002, as its inner ring.
#   B  Courtyard Hall, relation 7002 (building=yes): outer way 6003 at
#      x 520..760, y 100..300, courtyard way 6004 at x 580..700, y 150..250.
#   C  Two Halves Wood, relation 7003 (landuse=forest): one ring made of the
#      open ways 6005 and 6006, x 90..430, y 450..700.
#   D  Broken Wood, relation 7004: the ways 6007 + 6008 never close, so the
#      relation is invalid and is not filled.

window 1200 800
load_osm docs/screenshots/fixtures/multipolygon.osm
viewport 40.7120 -74.0060 18
wait_idle 5s
capture out/multipolygon-01-drawn.png

# Double-click in the water: the relation is selected (tinted, members in
# purple), not the lake's outer way.
click 170,250 count=2
wait_idle 2s
assert_selected relation 7001
capture out/multipolygon-02-lake-selected.png

# Double-click on the island: the island is a hole of the lake, so it is the
# island's own way that is selected.
click 260,215 count=2
wait_idle 2s
assert_selected way 6002
capture out/multipolygon-03-island-selected.png

# The building's walls, then its courtyard (a hole: the courtyard's own way).
click 540,200 count=2
wait_idle 2s
assert_selected relation 7002
capture out/multipolygon-04-building-selected.png
click 640,200 count=2
wait_idle 2s
assert_selected way 6004
capture out/multipolygon-05-courtyard-selected.png

# A ring made of two ways is one area.
click 260,575 count=2
wait_idle 2s
assert_selected relation 7003
capture out/multipolygon-06-two-way-ring-selected.png

# The broken relation has no fill to double-click.
click 700,585 count=2
wait_idle 2s
assert_selected none
capture out/multipolygon-07-broken-not-selectable.png

# Move a lake corner node: the fill follows the drag and the commit.
click 430,220
wait_idle 2s
assert_selected node 6104
drag 430,220 480,180 button=left
wait_idle 2s
capture out/multipolygon-08-corner-dragged.png

# One undo puts the corner back.
key cmd+z
wait_idle 2s
capture out/multipolygon-09-drag-undone.png

log done
